A||||4||docprego||Rear spoiler removal ||||5||
Z||000000||docprego||03-06-2001||01:09 AM||||Hello,<P>I am currently in the hunt for an 86-88 GT, love the fastback look.  BUT, I don't like the look of the rear spoiler on this body style.  IMHO it looks way sleeker without the spoiler. <P>So....If I find my perfect GT except that it has the rear spoiler, what can I do?<P>I would imagine I could remove the spoiler, but wouldn't that leave some nasty holes in the rear deck lid?<P>What solutions exist for this situation? Obviously I could get a replacement rear deck lid-if I can find another that was not originally equipped with the spoiler, but then the issue of color matching rears it's head.<P>Thanks for any ideas..<P>docprego.<P>P.S.  Anyone out there live in las Vegas and want to sell me a 86-88 GT?<p>[This message has been edited by docprego (edited 03-06-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||03-06-2001||08:49 AM||||Two options as I see it.  After spoiler removal, patch holes and repaint.  Search for holess GT decklid, same color if you are lucky, or repaint decklid.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rodmcneill||03-06-2001||10:31 AM||||The wing was an option that most people ordered but there are GTs out there with no wing. I personally like the wing myself although it does cut down on rear window visibility. Good luck finding your Fiero, at least in that area you don't have to worry about frame rust just paint fade.||||reg||1
Z||000003||docprego||03-07-2001||01:47 AM||||Just thought I would follow up with this:<P>Found a guy in Vegas today who said he had an 88 GT on his lot and about 10 Fieros in total.<P>I drove out to his lot in the middle of nowhere (in the pouring rain) and sure enough he had a GT, but it was an 85 notchback.  Not what I am looking for, but in good condition (only visible problem was that the chin spoiler was pushed in on the driver's side).  He also had not 10 other Fieros but 4-5 around this lot in various conditions.  There was one white 84 coupe in awesome condition, but 125K on the odometer.<P>If you want the guys name I can get it to you, he own's a repair shop in Vegas and sells cars off the same property ( I saw the Fieros at his storage lot in North Las Vegas).<P>My search for my GT continues...<P>docprego<p>[This message has been edited by docprego (edited 03-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||c m west||03-07-2001||07:28 PM||||keep in mind that without the spoiler that the torsion rods that support the decklid will want to act as a catapult without the weight of the spoiler - either swap out to smaller ones, say from a 4 cyl, or just be very carefull and make sure that the decklid limiting straps are in good condition<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> ||||reg||1
